   "text": "fp32, gemmv1: M / M(gemm1 fit in this session) against the desk model's 0.419 / 0.75 = 0.559. PASS in [0.35, 0.78]. Else FAIL.",
   "band": [
    0.35,
    0.78
   ]
  },
  "R3_tie": {
   "text": "fp32, gemm1 in this session against E101's fit: C within 30 cycles of 344.3 and M within 0.08 us of 0.838. Else the new binary is not the old arm: everything else is labelled.",
   "c": 30,
   "m": 0.08
  },
  "R4_gap_fp32_bycol": {
   "text": "fp32, gemmc1, zeros / sparse25, sustained rate. COMES BACK: ratio >= 1.15 and >= clock ratio - 0.03. STAYS GONE: ratio < 1.10. Else PARTIAL. E101's as-run sparse25 and randn gaps, with their clock gaps, stand beside it. The same with randn only if the rule admitted it.",
